1
00:00:00,105 --> 00:00:03,857
Loupe is a private library for the photographs that inspire you.

2
00:00:04,158 --> 00:00:07,776
This recording drives the real Angular application against the real

3
00:00:07,776 --> 00:00:12,342
API, worker, and database, signing in with a locally provisioned

4
00:00:12,342 --> 00:00:13,002
account.

5
00:00:14,625 --> 00:00:19,138
Inspiration opens on the whole collection: fifteen references across

6
00:00:19,138 --> 00:00:20,100
three boards.

7
00:00:20,402 --> 00:00:24,204
Boards and their counts sit in the sidebar, the most used tags line

8
00:00:24,204 --> 00:00:29,035
up above the grid, and hovering a card reveals its title, photographer,

9
00:00:29,349 --> 00:00:31,179
and a link to the original source.

10
00:00:32,772 --> 00:00:34,721
Saving starts from one button.

11
00:00:35,022 --> 00:00:39,009
Upload an image and Loupe reads it, shows a preview, and asks for

12
00:00:39,009 --> 00:00:40,682
a title and photographer.

13
00:00:40,983 --> 00:00:44,575
Tick a board, save, and the reference appears at the front of the

14
00:00:44,575 --> 00:00:46,918
library with the board count updated.

15
00:00:48,532 --> 00:00:50,402
Boards organise the library.

16
00:00:50,703 --> 00:00:54,282
Create a new board, then add references to it straight from their

17
00:00:54,282 --> 00:00:55,047
cards.

18
00:00:55,361 --> 00:00:59,374
The sidebar count follows each change, and opening the board shows

19
00:00:59,374 --> 00:01:00,836
only what belongs there.

20
00:01:02,452 --> 00:01:04,125
Tags work as filters.

21
00:01:04,426 --> 00:01:08,057
Choosing window light narrows the collection to the references carrying

22
00:01:08,057 --> 00:01:11,519
that tag, and the chip stays pressed until it is cleared.

23
00:01:11,821 --> 00:01:14,454
Clearing the tag restores the full library.

24
00:01:16,052 --> 00:01:20,881
Every reference has its own page: the full image, photographer, boards,

25
00:01:20,881 --> 00:01:23,804
source and attribution, tags and notes.

26
00:01:24,105 --> 00:01:28,342
Adding a tag saves straight away, and notes save with one click, so

27
00:01:28,342 --> 00:01:30,725
the context travels with the photograph.

28
00:01:32,332 --> 00:01:34,873
Search covers everything you have saved.

29
00:01:35,187 --> 00:01:39,661
Keyword search matches the words you typed, across titles, notes,

30
00:01:39,661 --> 00:01:42,439
tags, attribution, and photographers.

31
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:46,819
Searching for a photographer's name returns the photographer alongside

32
00:01:46,819 --> 00:01:48,702
the references that credit them.

33
00:01:50,292 --> 00:01:53,399
Results narrow by type, boards, and tags.

34
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:57,397
Searching for light and filtering to the Architecture board leaves

35
00:01:57,397 --> 00:02:00,504
only the architecture references that mention light.

36
00:02:00,805 --> 00:02:04,634
Opening a result lands on the reference page, with the tag added a

37
00:02:04,634 --> 00:02:05,570
moment ago.

38
00:02:07,185 --> 00:02:11,725
Everything shown was saved for real: the upload, the board, the tags

39
00:02:11,725 --> 00:02:15,476
and the note are in the database, and search found them a moment later.

40
00:02:15,791 --> 00:02:20,172
That is the Inspiration library today: browse, save, organise, and

41
00:02:20,172 --> 00:02:20,845
find.
